cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ha-taggle in your work, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "ha-taggle: receive-only Taggle water-meter decoder for Home Assistant"
authors:
  - name: "ha-taggle contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Spicynostalgia/ha-taggle"
url: "https://ha-taggle.dancloud.au"
version: "0.3.1"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Open-source, receive-only decoder for supported Taggle water-meter radio
  transmissions near 922 MHz in Australia. Uses RTL-SDR to decode DSSS/BPSK
  signals and publishes hourly pulse usage through MQTT to Home Assistant.
  Manual dial readings calibrate litres and starting offset. Only one
  transmitter in Gladstone, Queensland, has field confirmation with an RTL-SDR
  Blog V4. Other models and regions are unverified. Encrypted message bodies
  are not decrypted. Includes a receiver add-on, Docker and Python CLI routes,
  and a dashboard card distributed as a HACS custom repository.
keywords:
  - Taggle
  - water meter
  - Home Assistant
  - RTL-SDR
  - MQTT
  - Australia
  - DSSS
  - BPSK
